        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(exec): require approval for OpenClaw lifecycle commands",
        "body": "﻿﻿Fixes #99518\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where exec commands through gateway or node hosts could let OpenClaw gateway/daemon lifecycle mutations pass through normal allowlist or auto-review paths when they should require explicit approval.\n\nThe affected workflow is OpenClaw self-management from exec surfaces: stopping, starting, restarting, running, deleting, or uninstalling the gateway/daemon through CLI, launchctl, systemctl, schtasks, process-kill, shell-wrapper, package-manager, Windows shim, `env -S`, `xargs`/`find`, `sudo`/`doas`, and dispatch-wrapper commands.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a focused lifecycle classifier to the exec approval policy and wires it into the main gateway-host, node-host, and direct `system.run` approval paths. The guard forces explicit approval for OpenClaw lifecycle mutations unless exec is already in yolo mode (`security=full`, `ask=off`).\n\nForeground gateway runtime forms such as `openclaw gateway`, `openclaw gateway run`, `openclaw gateway restart`, and `openclaw gateway --force restart` are treated as lifecycle mutations. Read-only inspection remains outside the guard, including `openclaw gateway status`, `openclaw gateway --help`, `openclaw gateway run --help`, `launchctl print`, `systemctl status`, `schtasks /Query`, and generic read-only process lookups. `openclaw gateway call` is method-aware: lifecycle RPCs such as `update.run` and `gateway.restart.request` require explicit lifecycle approval, while read-only RPCs such as `health`, `update.status`, and `logs.tail` do not.\n\nThe classifier also handles lifecycle commands hidden behind common command carriers, including nested `env`, `env -S`, shell wrappers, package runners, `find`/`xargs`, process-kill pipelines, known environment expansions, unknown partial environments that could expand to OpenClaw, and Node launcher forms without treating benign `node -e` / `node --print` script arguments as executable paths. The classifier remains out of `openclaw/plugin-sdk/infra-runtime`; the deprecated SDK shim now explicitly preserves the previous exec approval exports without exposing this internal lifecycle taxonomy as plugin API.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators get an extra human confirmation before an agent or auto-review path can stop, start, restart, run, delete, or uninstall the OpenClaw gateway/daemon in non-yolo configurations. Existing yolo-mode behavior, read-only status/query commands, and public plugin SDK export counts are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFinal branch head: `60c5d3e36085b90715022d8bd823a2fdc0e72aa8`  \nRebased onto upstream `main`: `bdfe2a4e60d344d89f946efbb26d6f6046a48258`\n\n### Final-head live Gateway proof\n\nA production build from the final head was started as an isolated loopback Gateway with temporary config/state and `auth=none`. The proof driver imported the production `processGatewayAllowlist` implementation from the same head. Port, temporary path, request id, and device identity were redacted.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"branchHead\": \"60c5d3e36085b90715022d8bd823a2fdc0e72aa8\",\n  \"surface\": \"production processGatewayAllowlist with isolated config/state\",\n  \"gatewayHealth\": \"healthy\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"non-yolo lifecycle mutation\",\n      \"command\": \"openclaw gateway restart\",\n      \"security\": \"full\",\n      \"ask\": \"on-miss\",\n      \"autoReviewCalls\": 0,\n      \"outcome\": \"forced onto explicit-approval registration before auto-review; the fresh isolated Gateway then rejected the unpaired scope upgrade\",\n      \"hasLifecycleWarning\": true,\n      \"warning\": \"OpenClaw lifecycle commands require explicit approval unless exec is running in yolo mode.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"yolo lifecycle control\",\n      \"command\": \"openclaw gateway restart\",\n      \"security\": \"full\",\n      \"ask\": \"off\",\n      \"autoReviewCalls\": 0,\n      \"pendingStatus\": null,\n      \"deniedStatus\": null,\n      \"hasLifecycleWarning\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"read-only control\",\n      \"command\": \"openclaw gateway status\",\n      \"security\": \"full\",\n      \"ask\": \"on-miss\",\n      \"autoReviewCalls\": 0,\n      \"pendingStatus\": null,\n      \"deniedStatus\": null,\n      \"hasLifecycleWarning\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThis demonstrates the requested final-head boundary: the non-yolo lifecycle mutation cannot reach auto-review, while the yolo mutation and read-only command retain their control behavior. The isolated device was intentionally not paired, so this proof does not claim that a human approved the request after registration. Maintainer confirmation of the intended non-yolo policy remains a separate product/security decision.\n\n### Focused tests\n\n```shell\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/infra/exec-approvals-lifecycle-positive-a.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/exec-approvals-lifecycle-positive-b.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/exec-approvals-lifecycle-env.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/exec-approvals-lifecycle-shell.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/exec-approvals-lifecycle-negative.test.ts\n# Test Files  5 passed (5)\n# Tests       525 passed (525)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-gateway.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-node.test.ts \\\n  src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts \\\n  src/utils/utils-misc.test.ts \\\n  --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|gateway lifecycle RPC|durable allowlist|empty env operands|removes POSIX backslash line continuations\"\n# Test Files  4 passed (4)\n# Tests       9 passed | 229 skipped (238)\n```\n\n### Static and CI validation\n\n- Changed-file `oxfmt --check`: passed.\n- Changed-file type-aware `oxlint`: passed.\n- `pnpm check:max-lines-ratchet --base bdfe2a4e60d344d89f946efbb26d6f6046a48258`: passed.\n- `git diff --check bdfe2a4e60d344d89f946efbb26d6f6046a48258...HEAD`: passed.\n- Linux Node 24 `check-test-types`: passed.\n- CI max-lines ratchet, lint, production types, security checks, QA smoke profiles, and real behavior proof: passed.\n\nThe remaining red CI shard is an unrelated timeout in untouched `src/cli/acp-cli-exit.process.test.ts`; all other compact shards passed.\n\r\n",
